# PARKED: this file is not active. GitHub reads code owners only from a file named exactly
# `CODEOWNERS`, in `.github/`, the root, or `docs/`, so the `.draft` suffix keeps it out of
# that lookup and out of the settings page, placeholder owners and all. It is kept rather
# than deleted for the path list below.
#
# To activate, in this order: substitute a real team or handle for every
# `@REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS`, rename to `.github/CODEOWNERS`, then enable
# "Require review from Code Owners".

# CODEOWNERS — review ownership for high-blast-radius paths.
#
# @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS is a placeholder, not a real handle. It is written to
# be unmistakable in GitHub's own "not a valid owner" error, because that is where it will
# be read: while flipping a branch-protection toggle, not while reading this file.
# Substitute the real reviewing team or handles first. Enabling "Require review from Code
# Owners" while the placeholder is here blocks every pull request touching these paths.
#
# This file is advisory on its own: GitHub only auto-requests these owners and does not
# block a merge unless "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in the branch-protection
# rule. Enable that toggle, or these entries are a suggestion, not a gate.
#
# Each line: <path-pattern>   <owner(s)>. Later matches win, so order from broad to specific.
#
# Inclusion test — one question: *would a silent change here weaken a guarantee that nothing
# else re-checks?* That is why the list below owns the gate's implementation and not only its
# declaration: most of ci.yml's jobs are thin `run: ./scripts/ci-local.sh <leg>` wrappers, so
# the workflows describe the gate while that script is the gate, and editing it silently
# weakens every job that delegates to it.

# --- The gate itself: these decide whether anything else is actually checked -------------
/scripts/ci-local.sh               @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/scripts/check-ci-gate.py          @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/scripts/vendored.sh               @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/.githooks/                        @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# The chokepoint lint: `disallowed-methods` here is what binds fixes such as the
# redirect-SSRF one, so relaxing an entry silently un-fixes it at every call site at once.
/clippy.toml                       @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- CI / release pipeline: build, sign, publish, supply-chain gates ----------------------
/.github/workflows/                @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# Controls whether dependency updates are proposed at all; narrowing it stops the freshness
# net without any check going red.
/.github/dependabot.yml            @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- Supply chain: what actually gets compiled in and shipped ----------------------------
/deny.toml                         @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# The resolved dependency closure. A lock change is a supply-chain change, and it is the one
# artifact `cargo deny` reads; reviewing it is the point, Dependabot churn included.
/Cargo.lock                        @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# The hash-locked Python closure for the conformance + crypt4gh oracles (CI-only, never
# shipped, but fetched and executed on the runner).
/conformance/requirements.lock     @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/conformance/requirements-crypt4gh.lock  @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# The single container-image definition (both the recompile and byte-identical `prebuilt`
# release paths) and the digest-pinned cross-rs containers that compile the SLSA-attested
# release binaries.
/Dockerfile                        @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/Cross.toml                        @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# The compiler pin. It outranks `rustup default`, so it is what every gated `cargo` actually
# builds with, and what the Dockerfile builder must match.
/rust-toolchain.toml               @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# Third-party licence attribution: what ships in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md and in the image.
/about.toml                        @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/about.hbs                         @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- Disclosure control: the privacy guarantee this node exists to make -------------------
# k-anonymity thresholds and the suppression decision. A quiet change here does not fail any
# test that does not already know the new threshold — it just discloses more.
/crates/core/src/kanon.rs          @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
# Population-field parsing/authority: what counts as AC/AF/AN and which population a count is
# attributed to; feeds the suppression maths above.
/crates/core/src/popfield.rs       @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- Cryptography: at-rest and in-transit ------------------------------------------------
/crates/core/src/crypt4gh/         @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- Frozen external contracts: a regression here is a public-API break -------------------
/conformance/shapes/               @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
/conformance/ga4gh-beacon-v2/      @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS

# --- Production deployment ---------------------------------------------------------------
/deploy/kubernetes/                @REPLACE-BEFORE-ENABLING-CODEOWNERS
